      Disables device tree nodes in the FDT passed to the next boot stage if the current domain lacks MMIO access to the device's first register block. Operates at whole-device granularity: it checks only reg[0] and disables the entire node via status="disabled". If the domain HAS IMSIC access (so the node is NOT disabled) but the IOMMU later creates a superpage GPA mapping that spans individual interrupt-file pages within that device's MMIO range, this fixup provides no protection — the device remains visible to the next stage, and the IOMMU translation is not constrained. The function correctly serves its FDT-fixup purpose, but the architectural assumption that 'domain MMIO access = safe IOMMU mapping' is unverified.
